citeturn0search26 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 1.1 years ago; Many results in graph theory, starting with Menger's theorem, guarantee the existence of paths or cycles in a k-connected graph. ... After the conjecture was made, it was proven for k = 4 by Péter L. ... Woodall's paper included a proof that the conclusion of the conjecture holds if G is (2k − 2)-connected, and in 1977, Thomassen proved that the conjecture holds if G is (3k − 1)/2-connected.
